Subject: Qt 6.10.2: tolerate an absent PipeWire loop during capture cleanup

Local correction approved for AutoTalk's bundled library on 2026-09-29.
This is not the upstream CoreEventListener lifetime fix.

When OpenPipeWireRemote fails, the response handler still transitions to
Streaming although open() never allocated m_threadLoop. stop() and destruction
must tolerate this partially initialized state. All other teardown stays intact.
Reproducer: tests/probes/qt_remote_failure.py (stock Qt exits with SIGSEGV).

